  "decisions": [
    {
      "concept": "selector",
      "note": "The committed render declares `device.selector_type: LinearServoSelector` (the same on `[mmu_unit unit0]`), with ERCF's real selector hardware coupled to it: `selector_stepper: unit0_selector`, `selector_servo: unit0_selector_servo`, `encoder: unit0`. That is what Happy Hare's family Kconfig specifies -- `if MMU_FAMILY_ERCF` does `imply LINEAR_SERVO_SELECTOR` and `select MMU_HAS_ENCODER` (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:6-8) -- and the version choice is nested under that family, so this dossier is traced with `MMU_FAMILY_ERCF` + `MMU_TYPE_ERCF_1_1` (plus the MMB 2.0 shared-exit symbols). A bare `MMU_TYPE_ERCF_1_1` without the family renders Happy Hare's 'Safety' VirtualSelector instead. Rendered selector motion: `selector_move_speed: 200`, `selector_homing_speed: 60`, `selector_accel: 1200`, `servo_buzz_gear_on_down: 3`, `servo_move_angle: 30`. klipper-mmu drives it as a LINEAR selector with a grip servo (`KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_KIND_LINEAR`, `KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_LINEAR_HAS_SERVO`): the carriage homes to its endstop before the first selection and after a fault, moves at the same 200 mm/s (60 mm/s homing, 1200 mm/s^2), and the servo grips at 100 degrees, releases at 30 and travels at 30, driven by Klipper's scheduled software PWM on any GPIO (`KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_SERVO`). Gate positions start from an estimate computed from Happy Hare's CAD geometry (`4.2,25.2,46.2,72.2,93.2,114.2,140.2,161.2,182.2` mm) until `KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE_SELECTOR` measures the real ones. ERCF 1.1's Springy, Triple Decky and Binky options are offered in menuconfig (`KLIPPER_MMU_ERCF_SPRINGY`, `KLIPPER_MMU_ERCF_TRIPLE_DECKY`, `KLIPPER_MMU_ERCF_BINKY`). Software candidate: it builds and passes the simulators, but has not run on real hardware."
    },
    {
      "concept": "arrival",
      "note": "LOAD completes and arrival is encoder-measured, not blind: after the bowden feed the extruder approach is a collision-homing loop of nine 2.4 mm moves (`operations.load.moves`; each step is 2.4 mm = 3.0 x ceil(0.7059 x 10)/10 for the 0.7059 mm TCRT5000 count) followed by the final 'Loading filament to nozzle' push, and the operation ends at `operations.load.end.tip = 789.774300`, `filament_pos: 10`, `gate_status: 1`, `errors: []`. The render configures `extruder_homing_endstop: encoder`, `gate_homing_endstop: encoder`, `gate_endstop_to_encoder: 10`, `encoder_move_validation: 1`, `bowden_allowable_encoder_delta: 20.0`, `skip_cal_encoder: 0`. The recorded end-stop read-out is empty for all five operations here (`end.sensor: null`, `end.offset: null`), where 2.0/3.0 record `mmu_entry` / 137.577 and `mmu_entry` / 134.121 on EJECT."
    },
    {
      "concept": "encoder",
      "note": "An encoder is bound (`encoder: unit0`) and its checks are on: `encoder_move_validation: 1`, `bowden_allowable_encoder_delta: 20.0`, `skip_cal_encoder: 0`, `gate_endstop_to_encoder: 10`, with both `gate_homing_endstop` and `extruder_homing_endstop` set to `encoder`. The render does not name the physical part; ERCF 1.1's Kconfig default is a TCRT5000 opto (Binky-8 only with the MOD_BINKY mod, installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:180-186), i.e. the 0.7059 mm/count device the harness models -- and the resolution is what makes this device's collision homing converge. 2.0's Binky-8 (1.469 mm) and 3.0's Binky-12 (0.979 mm) fail the same loop (see version_diff). klipper-mmu turns its encoder input on by default for every ERCF (`KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER`, because Happy Hare's ERCF family selects MMU_HAS_ENCODER): a one-wire click counter on `KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_ENCODER_A`, which needs that pin and `KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER_PULL` set before the image starts. It is used for clog detection (no click over `KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER_DETECTION_LENGTH_MM`, 10 mm, of gear travel), for progress checks during an operation, and to measure the Bowden length with `KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE` when a toolhead switch is fitted. Happy Hare's encoder homing (`gate_homing_endstop: encoder`) is not a klipper-mmu mode: LOAD ends at a local toolhead switch or at FPS arrival."
    },
    {
      "concept": "buffer_type",
      "note": "No `[mmu_buffer unit0]` renders and no buffer key appears anywhere in the dossier, although the family Kconfig implies `MMU_HAS_FILAMENT_BUFFER` (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:9). klipper-mmu has no 'no buffer' build: every image follows the extruder from a buffer input -- a switched pair (`KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_BUFFER_A/B`), a single tension switch (`KLIPPER_MMU_BUFFER_SINGLE_SWITCH`) or the analog DiffA/DiffB pair, so an ERCF build needs one wired even though this render declares none."
    },
    {
      "concept": "preload_park",
      "note": "PRELOAD ends at `operations.preload.end.tip = -2.882600` with `gate_preload_parking_distance: -23` and an empty `gate_preload_endstop`, and SELECT leaves the filament there (`operations.select.end.tip = -2.882600`). The -23 is ERCF 1.1's own default (-13 with Thumper blocks, installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:174-176)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "unload_park",
      "note": "UNLOAD re-homes to the same park: `operations.unload.end.tip = -2.647500` with `gate_parking_distance: -23`, `filament_pos: 0`, `gate_status: 2`, `errors: []`. 1.1's -23 is the version's own value; 2.0 parks -13 (-11 with Thumper blocks, Kconfig.ercf:220-222) and 3.0 -16 (Kconfig.ercf:264)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "eject_extra",
      "note": "EJECT adds a flat `gate_final_eject_distance: 20` mm past the park with homing off, ending at `operations.eject.end.tip = -22.647500` (`filament_pos: 0`, `gate_status: 0`, `errors: []`)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "version_diff",
      "note": "The three versions are no longer identical renders, and their recorded behaviour differs. This one (1.1): 9 gates, `show_bypass: 0`, `gear_ratio: 80:20` -> `steps_per_mm: 563.090637`, `servo_move_angle: 30`, parking -23, no `gate_autoload`, no per-gate entry sensor, PRELOAD/UNLOAD end tips -2.883/-2.648, EJECT tip -22.648, LOAD ending at `filament_pos: 10` with no errors. 2.0: 8 gates, `show_bypass: 1`, 80:20 (same `steps_per_mm`), `servo_move_angle: 50`, parking -13, `gate_autoload: 1`, per-gate `mmu_entry_switch_pin_0..7`, end tips 6.717/7.577/-12.423, and LOAD/UNLOAD/EJECT each end with the recorded error 'Failed to reach extruder encoder endstop after moving 112.5mm'. 3.0: 8 gates, `show_bypass: 1`, `gear_ratio: 1:1` -> `steps_per_mm: 140.772659`, `servo_move_angle: 50`, parking -16, `gate_autoload: 1`, per-gate entry sensors, end tips 4.210/4.121/-15.879, and the same error at 117.0mm. Encoder defaults by version: TCRT5000 / Binky-8 / Binky-12 (Kconfig.ercf:180-186, :224-231, :267-274). The 2.0/3.0 failure tracks the encoder model, not the machine: controlled probes hold it to the encoder choice alone -- 1.1 with Binky-8 fails identically at 112.5 mm, and 2.0/3.0 with TCRT5000 complete on either board (EASY_BRD_RP2040 or MMB_2_0) -- the harness collision-homing loop cannot converge at the coarser Binky step. The devices' real encoders are kept as shipped; swapping them to TCRT5000 to make the harness pass would falsify the hardware. v3.0's optional Jack Rabbit mod renders a plain `LinearSelector` (no servo) and sets `filament_always_gripped` (Kconfig.ercf:98-105); it is not selected here."
    }
